{"id_": "1fc3730b-18f3-4cd1-b437-2b66ce90897f", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"pubmed_id": "25277731", "question": "Sternal fracture in growing children : A rare and often overlooked fracture?", "final_decision": "maybe"}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": [], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": [], "relationships": {}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "
", "text": "Sternal fractures in childhood are rare. The aim of the study was to investigate the accident mechanism, the detection of radiological and sonographical criteria and consideration of associated injuries. In the period from January 2010 to December 2012 all inpatients and outpatients with sternal fractures were recorded according to the documentation. A total of 4 children aged 5-14 years with a sternal fracture were treated in 2 years, 2 children were hospitalized for pain management and 2 remained in outpatient care. BACKGROUND METHOD RESULTS Adolescent Chest Pain Child Child, Preschool Diagnosis, Differential Fractures, Bone Humans Male Rare Diseases Sternum m a y b e m a y b e", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": null, "end_char_idx": null, "text_template": "{metadata_str}

