", "text": "A difference in the incidence of cancer was only detectable after a 4 year lag and progressively increased with continued follow-up. On multivariable analysis the colon cancer risk in patients who received bezafibrate tended to be lower with a hazard ratio of 0.47 and 95% confidence interval 0.2-1.1. BACKGROUND METHODS RESULTS Aged Bezafibrate Colonic Neoplasms Coronary Artery Disease Dose-Response Relationship, Drug Female Follow-Up Studies Humans Hypolipidemic Agents Incidence Kaplan-Meier Estimate Ligands Longitudinal Studies Male Middle Aged Multivariate Analysis Peroxisome Proliferator-Activated Receptors Randomized Controlled Trials as Topic y e s y e s", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": null, "end_char_idx": null, "text_template": "{metadata_str}

