", "text": "The minimum followup was 12 months (median, 56 months; range, 12-108 months). Compared with patients having above-knee amputation, patients undergoing limb-salvage surgery had superior Physiological Cost Index scores and Reintegration to Normal Living Index. The Toronto Extremity Salvage scores and SF-36 scores were similar in the two groups. INTRODUCTION PURPOSES METHODS RESULTS Activities of Daily Living Adolescent Adult Aged Amputation Amputees Artificial Limbs Bone Neoplasms Female Humans Limb Salvage Lower Extremity Male Middle Aged Patient Selection Perception Prosthesis Fitting Quality of Life Recovery of Function Retrospective Studies Soft Tissue Neoplasms Surveys and Questionnaires Texas Time Factors Treatment Outcome Young Adult y e s m a y b e", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": null, "end_char_idx": null, "text_template": "{metadata_str}

