", "text": "Delay in transfer to rehabilitation was associated with a longer total hospital length of stay of 0.64 (95% CI 0.23-1.05) days per day of delay in transfer. AIMS METHODS RESULTS Aged Aged, 80 and over Female Femoral Neck Fractures Hospital Units Humans Length of Stay Logistic Models Male Patient Transfer Rehabilitation Centers Risk Factors Time Factors y e s y e s", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": null, "end_char_idx": null, "text_template": "{metadata_str}

