", "text": "C reactive protein values of patients with PID were also noted. MPV values in patients with PID were lower than those in the control group. This reduction in MPV is statistically significant when the PID patient group is compared with the control group (p < 0.001). A negative correlation was discovered between platelet count and MPV values (p = 0.019, r = - 0.425). Receiver-operating curve analysis pointed out that MPV has greater area under curve value than neutrophil rate, leukocyte and platelet count (0.73, 0.64, 0.72 and 0.49 respectively). BACKGROUND METHODS RESULTS Adult Biomarkers Blood Sedimentation C-Reactive Protein Case-Control Studies Early Diagnosis Female Humans Mean Platelet Volume Pelvic Inflammatory Disease Platelet Count Predictive Value of Tests y e s y e s", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": null, "end_char_idx": null, "text_template": "{metadata_str}

