", "text": "Duration of AF ≥ 38 months (p = 0.01), left atrial diameter ≥ 54 mm (0.001), left atrial area ≥ 33 cm(2) (p = 0.005), absence of connecting lesions (p= 0.04), and absence of right atrial ablation (p<0.001) were independently associated with high incidence of AF recurrence. In contrast the absence of GP ablation was not a significant factor (p = 0.12). BACKGROUND METHODS RESULTS Aged Atrial Fibrillation Autonomic Denervation Autonomic Nervous System Catheter Ablation Female Heart Rate Humans Male Middle Aged Pericardium Postoperative Period Retrospective Studies n o n o", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": null, "end_char_idx": null, "text_template": "{metadata_str}

