", "text": "The concept of a HSK was generally viewed as positive, with many benefits identified relating to increased access to testing, enhanced personal comfort and empowerment. Concerns about the accuracy of the test, delays in receiving the results, the possible lack of support and potential negative impact on 'others' were raised. OBJECTIVE METHODS RESULTS Adult Bisexuality Feasibility Studies Focus Groups Health Knowledge, Attitudes, Practice Homosexuality, Male Humans Interviews as Topic Male Mass Screening Middle Aged Patient Acceptance of Health Care Qualitative Research Reagent Kits, Diagnostic Risk-Taking Sexually Transmitted Diseases United Kingdom Young Adult m a y b e y e s", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": null, "end_char_idx": null, "text_template": "{metadata_str}

