", "text": "The number of general practitioner visits among women and men significantly increased from 2001 to 2009 (women: OR 1.43, 1.27-1.61; men: OR 1.71, 1.49-1.97). OBJECTIVES STUDY DESIGN OUTCOME MEASURES RESULTS Aged Aged, 80 and over Female Health Care Surveys Health Services Health Status Hospitalization Humans Logistic Models Male Odds Ratio Office Visits Patient Acceptance of Health Care Polypharmacy Prevalence Self Report Socioeconomic Factors Spain y e s y e s", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": null, "end_char_idx": null, "text_template": "{metadata_str}

