", "text": "Chewable and dispersible tablets (P<0.001), gastrointestinal medicines (P = 0.002) and antibiotics (P = 0.007) were significant predictors of higher pH. In contrast, effervescent tablets (P<0.001), and nutrition and blood preparations (P = 0.021) were significant predictors of higher titratable acidity. OBJECTIVE METHODS RESULTS Child Child, Preschool Drug-Related Side Effects and Adverse Reactions Humans Hydrogen-Ion Concentration Metabolic Clearance Rate Mouth Pharmaceutical Preparations Pharmaceutical Vehicles Sucrose Sweetening Agents Titrimetry Tooth Erosion n o n o", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": null, "end_char_idx": null, "text_template": "{metadata_str}

